      "description": "Watch Heart Of Midlothian vs Benfica highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. The atmosphere was electric at Tynecastle as Heart of Midlothian welcomed Portuguese giants Benfica for a high-stakes UEFA Europa League clash. Both sides looked to establish dominance early in a match that promised intensity and tactical intrigue from the first whistle. A Gritty Opening Exchange On August 13, 2026, the contest began with both teams testing each other's defensive resolve. Heart of Midlothian showed no fear against their illustrious opponents, maintaining a disciplined shape and closing down spaces. The first half was characterized by physical battles in midfield, punctuated by a yellow card for Claudio Braga in the 34th minute as the home side fought to keep Benfica at bay. Despite the pressure from the visitors, the score remained deadlocked as the referee blew for halftime. Tactical Shifts and the Second Half The second half saw the Benfica manager look to his bench to break the stalemate, introducing Tomas Araujo for Clement Lenglet immediately after the break. The game remained a tense affair until the 64th minute, when a triple substitution brought Tomas Magnusson , Leandro Barreiro , and Gianluca Prestianni onto the pitch. These changes injected fresh energy into the Portuguese side’s attack, gradually wearing down the Hearts defense that had stood firm for over an hour. The Decisive Double Blow The deadlock was finally broken in the 77th minute when substitute Tomas Magnusson found the back of the net, silencing the home crowd. Before Heart of Midlothian could even catch their breath, Benfica struck again. Just two minutes later, Dodi Lukebakio doubled the lead with a clinical finish in the 79th minute. Although the Scottish side attempted to respond with their own set of substitutions, including the introduction of James Wilson and MJ Kamara , the visitors managed the closing stages with professional composure to secure the victory."
